# onioncrawler seed list - one URL per line, '#' starts a comment.
# ONLY .onion URLs are accepted (or .i2p when the crawler runs with --enable-i2p);
# every other host is refused (no clearnet leak). Replace these with real v3
# onion seeds before a real crawl.
#
# This same file works as the CURATED seed list for scheduled re-seeding:
#   onioncrawler reseed --db crawl.db --seed-list seeds.txt
#   onioncrawler crawl  --db crawl.db --seed-list seeds.txt --reseed-interval 21600
# Re-seeding validates + dedups + blocklist-checks these roots and re-enqueues
# them so the index keeps rediscovering them (respecting caps + recrawl).
#
# http://<56-char-base32>.onion/
# http://exampleexampleexampleexampleexampleexampleexampleexampl.onion/
